    "title": "Study links heart issues with high screen times in children - NewsBreak",
    "text": "HENDERSON, Ky. (WEHT) — A new study by the American heart Association says children and young adults who spend a lot of time looking at screens have an increased risk of high blood pressure, high cholesterol and insulin resistance. According to the study involving 1,000 people, it also found that sleep duration and timing affected the risk factors. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
